{"audio": "james-03.opus", "voice": "Davis", "duration_ms": 132933, "sentences": [{"start_ms": 0, "end_ms": 1200, "text": "James, Chapter Three."}, {"start_ms": 1200, "end_ms": 6533, "text": "My brethren, be not many masters, knowing that we shall receive the greater condemnation."}, {"start_ms": 6533, "end_ms": 8933, "text": "For in many things we offend all."}, {"start_ms": 8933, "end_ms": 14800, "text": "If any man offend not in word, the same is a perfect man, and able also to bridle the whole body."}, {"start_ms": 14800, "end_ms": 21067, "text": "Behold, we put bits in the horses' mouths, that they may obey us; and we turn about their whole body."}, {"start_ms": 21067, "end_ms": 31467, "text": "Behold also the ships, which though they be so great, and are driven of fierce winds, yet are they turned about with a very small helm, whithersoever the governor listeth."}, {"start_ms": 31467, "end_ms": 36400, "text": "Even so the tongue is a little member, and boasteth great things."}, {"start_ms": 36400, "end_ms": 39600, "text": "Behold, how great a matter a little fire kindleth!"}, {"start_ms": 39600, "end_ms": 53067, "text": "And the tongue is a fire, a world of iniquity: so is the tongue among our members, that it defileth the whole body, and setteth on fire the course of nature; and it is set on fire of hell."}, {"start_ms": 53067, "end_ms": 67333, "text": "For every kind of beasts, and of birds, and of serpents, and of things in the sea, is tamed, and hath been tamed of mankind: But the tongue can no man tame; it is an unruly evil, full of deadly poison."}, {"start_ms": 67333, "end_ms": 73733, "text": "Therewith bless we God, even the Father; and therewith curse we men, which are made after the similitude of God."}, {"start_ms": 73733, "end_ms": 76933, "text": "Out of the same mouth proceedeth blessing and cursing."}, {"start_ms": 76933, "end_ms": 80400, "text": "My brethren, these things ought not so to be."}, {"start_ms": 80400, "end_ms": 84400, "text": "Doth a fountain send forth at the same place sweet water and bitter?"}, {"start_ms": 84400, "end_ms": 87333, "text": "Can the fig tree, my brethren, bear olive berries?"}, {"start_ms": 87333, "end_ms": 89067, "text": "either a vine, figs?"}, {"start_ms": 89067, "end_ms": 93200, "text": "so can no fountain both yield salt water and fresh."}, {"start_ms": 93200, "end_ms": 96800, "text": "Who is a wise man and endued with knowledge among you?"}, {"start_ms": 96800, "end_ms": 100933, "text": "let him shew out of a good conversation his works with meekness of wisdom."}, {"start_ms": 100933, "end_ms": 106933, "text": "But if ye have bitter envying and strife in your hearts, glory not, and lie not against the truth."}, {"start_ms": 106933, "end_ms": 112933, "text": "This wisdom descendeth not from above, but is earthly, sensual, devilish."}, {"start_ms": 112933, "end_ms": 117733, "text": "For where envying and strife is, there is confusion and every evil work."}, {"start_ms": 117733, "end_ms": 128933, "text": "But the wisdom that is from above is first pure, then peaceable, gentle, and easy to be intreated, full of mercy and good fruits, without partiality, and without hypocrisy."}, {"start_ms": 128933, "end_ms": 132933, "text": "And the fruit of righteousness is sown in peace of them that make peace."}], "words": [{"t": "James,", "s": 102, "e": 447, "si": 0}, {"t": "Chapter", "s": 529, "e": 875, "si": 0}, {"t": "Three.", "s": 936, "e": 1180, "si": 0}, {"t": "My", "s": 1681, "e": 1781, "si": 1}, {"t": "brethren,", "s": 1842, "e": 2202, "si": 1}, {"t": "be", "s": 2383, "e": 2443, "si": 1}, {"t": "not", "s": 2543, "e": 2704, "si": 1}, {"t": "many", "s": 2744, "e": 2944, "si": 1}, {"t": "masters,", "s": 3024, "e": 3606, "si": 1}, {"t": "knowing", "s": 4027, "e": 4288, "si": 1}, {"t": "that", "s": 4308, "e": 4428, "si": 1}, {"t": "we", "s": 4468, "e": 4548, "si": 1}, {"t": "shall", "s": 4588, "e": 4769, "si": 1}, {"t": "receive", "s": 4809, "e": 5210, "si": 1}, {"t": "the", "s": 52